": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"04c4051b365f52958ad30f6d1bcaf7dd3fa8fc988506bb5c96f3520b86366e04","event_uuid":"5b1c60a1-4645-47a1-ada8-afc0ebf81d8a","position":{"commit_sha":"490bc5f9616c95c4ff9da29f753ecd665a40f619","position":"1787188178169070680-5b1c60a1-4645-47a1-ada8-afc0ebf81d8a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"S2a pushed for review as Gerrit change 1925 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1925).\n\nHeld-out oracle validated GREEN: restored the withheld edge/E2E tests (validation rejections, import isolation, non-terminating ParseError, alias/epilog composition) and folded them into the two file-impact-declared test files; full set = 38 passing. Gave the oracle teeth via mutation — terminating error() and disabled unknown_capability detection both drove held-out assertions RED, then restored to GREEN.\n\nTwo orchestrator reconciliations post-implementation:\n1. Dropped the subagent's per-file-ignores BLE001 carve-out in pyproject.toml; rewrote the immutability test to use pytest.raises(AttributeError) so no lint config change ships.\n2. Contract reconciliation on rebase onto current origin/main: the new bridge-vocabulary contract (test_help_overview_coverage.py::test_shipped_surfaces_name_no_retired_bridge_command) bans the retired token 'purge-bridge' from shipped package source. The registry had added a concrete Route('purge-bridge', retired=True) purely to exercise the retired mechanism. Removed it — the shipped ROUTES table now names no retired verb; the retired field/validation/derive-exclusion mechanism stays and is exercised on synthetic routes in the held-out validation oracle. Updated the hidden/retired test to assert route_for('purge-bridge') is None and no retired route ships (reinforcing the ban). Shadow-parity unaffected (retired routes were already excluded from derived sets).","timestamp":1787181948221256001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PS3: PS1/PS2 CI (Verified-1) surfaced a repo-wide contract I'd missed by running only the ticket's narrow verify commands. test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout::test_no_uncategorized_live_old_spelling scans ALL git-tracked files for legacy bridge spellings (bridge-fsck|bridge-probe|jira-onboard) and requires each retaining file to be in _COMPATIBILITY_FILES or immutable-history. My _registry.py necessarily names those live compat spellings (shadow-parity: the live _cli frozensets still route them), and test_cli_registry.py anchors on them - the same compatibility-surface category _cli/__init__.py and the other contract test files already occupy. Added src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py and tests/unit/test_cli_registry.py to _COMPATIBILITY_FILES. Verified locally: full bridge-vocabulary suite green + a 186-test sweep of source-scanning contracts/guards. The 6 other PS1 'failures' (doctor_dirty_tree, llm_failure_classifier) were artifacts of PS2's push canceling PS1's run mid-flight; they pass locally.","timestamp":1787185456387932001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"PS4 fixes a CI flake this change itself introduced (not pre-existing on origin/main). The S2a import-isolation test did sys.modules.pop('pydantic_ai', 'rebar_reconciler', ...) without restoring, poisoning the shared pytest-xdist worker — surfacing intermittently as 'module pydantic_ai has no attribute models' in test_pai_output/test_llm_failure_classifier and split-module-identity failures in test_doctor_dirty_tree (run A red / run B green on the same PS3 commit). Rewrote the check to run in a fresh subprocess (no global sys.modules mutation) and narrowed the forbidden set to the honest shadow-phase guarantee. Teeth: injecting an eager 'import pydantic_ai' into _registry drives it RED.","timestamp":1787187840502179001}],"created_at":1787070448141143001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7b85b53a-7c25-4ce1-ae1f-b7c6703fe77b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"},{"link_uuid":"1ddffefa-26a1-4606-b94e-bc6c9c126564","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ad61-0a0e-bb2e-4b36"},{"link_uuid":"230e94c9-9c2e-43a2-b6ca-5688fc45d7a1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fc45-7256-44f0-4300"},{"link_uuid":"3ae3d6bf-3f83-4d9f-b4c0-1032e419dd7b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0a03-f16e-a792-4e91"},{"link_uuid":"5b1c60a1-4645-47a1-ada8-afc0ebf81d8a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"af87-47a8-6341-4558"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nS2 needs a lean contract that can describe routes and locate one execution/help parser without importing handlers or optional dependencies. Existing command sets and parser styles cannot be migrated safely until factory, formatting, validation, and compatibility rules are fixed.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a stdlib-only CLI parser foundation and immutable route registry.\n\n- Define a narrow factory protocol equivalent to `build_parser(*, prog: str) -> argparse.ArgumentParser`.\n- Provide one Rebar ArgumentParser/formatter customization for deterministic width/order/newlines and compatibility-preserving parse errors/return control. It extends argparse; it does not define another grammar.\n- Let route records hold lazy handler and parser-factory references plus identity/alias/visibility/help, mount/init, confirmation/output, and possible-capability metadata.\n- Validate duplicate spellings, illegal alias/retired collisions, contradictory policies, unknown capability ids, malformed references, and resource/parser census state without resolving command handlers.\n- Derive the legacy policy-set exports from routes and run a shadow comparison against all current sets/arms. Do not cut help or execution over in this task.\n- Define reusable argument-definition composition for canonical/nested/compatibility spellings so aliases can vary `prog`/epilog without copying options.\n\nThe formatter policy is an explicit byte contract: fixed width independent of terminal, deterministic command/option ordering, UTF-8 LF output, and one trailing newline.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nNo public behavior changes. Existing help files and execution ladder remain authoritative. Reverting this task removes only unused expansion scaffolding.\n\n## Testing\nUse in-process unit tests with synthetic factories/routes. Observable oracles are exact formatted bytes, parse success/failure without process termination, deterministic validation findings, derived-set parity, and blocked imports proving registry construction resolves no handlers or optional packages.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The factory protocol and shared argparse customization produce deterministic help and compatibility-shaped parse errors from one parser object.\n- [ ] Frozen route records represent every current spelling and derive compatibility policy exports with zero shadow-census delta.\n- [ ] Registry validation rejects each synthetic duplicate, contradiction, unknown capability, malformed reference, and alias/retired collision deterministically.\n- [ ] Import blockers prove registry construction and route lookup import neither handlers nor optional dependencies.\n- [ ] No runtime help or execution path has cut over, and rollback is removal-only.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"Immutable route records, lazy handler/parser references, validation, and derived compatibility exports."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py","reason":"Shared stdlib argparse factory protocol, deterministic formatter, and compatibility error seam."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py","reason":"Shadow-only derived compatibility exports; no route cutover."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry.py","reason":"Pure route validation, lazy import, and census parity tests."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_parser_contract.py","reason":"Deterministic help and parse-error contract tests."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12"],["relates_to","0a03-f16e-a792-4e91"],["relates_to","ad61-0a0e-bb2e-4b36"],["relates_to","af87-47a8-6341-4558"],["relates_to","b06c-04a9-52b2-42fe"],["relates_to","fc45-7256-44f0-4300"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2635-4aa3-5c14-4b12","parent_status_uuid":"e53549f0-1053-4ec4-81c9-78f8c080fe79","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_id":"b2ff-03f7-a223-4900","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-05 S2a — Define the lean parser and route registry contract","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_cli_parser_contract.py tests/unit/test_cli_registry.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"Pure parser formatting, registry validation, lazy imports, and current-route shadow parity"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"No behavior cutover and repository structural policy"}]},"source_event_uuids":["3d6bb472-7c38-41f5-ad7e-146f0f5c34c2","e53549f0-1053-4ec4-81c9-78f8c080fe79","077f2d9d-2e27-42c8-a9b7-2f1